DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       ppccaapp__aaccttiivvaattee()  is used to activate a packet capture handle to look at
       packets on the network, with the options that were set  on  the  handle
       being in effect.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEE
       ppccaapp__aaccttiivvaattee() returns 00 on success without warnings, a non-zero posi‐
       tive value on success with warnings, and a negative value on error.   A
       non-zero  return  value  indicates  what warning or error condition oc‐
       curred.

       The possible warning values are:

       PPCCAAPP__WWAARRNNIINNGG__PPRROOMMIISSCC__NNOOTTSSUUPP
              Promiscuous mode was requested, but the capture  source  doesn't
              support promiscuous mode.

       PPCCAAPP__WWAARRNNIINNGG__TTSSTTAAMMPP__TTYYPPEE__NNOOTTSSUUPP
              The    time    stamp    type    specified    in    a    previous
              ppccaapp__sseett__ttssttaammpp__ttyyppee(3) call  isn't  supported  by  the  capture
              source (the time stamp type is left as the default),

       PPCCAAPP__WWAARRNNIINNGG
              Another  warning condition occurred; ppccaapp__ggeetteerrrr(3) or ppccaapp__ppeerr‐‐
              rroorr(3) may be called with _p as an argument to fetch or display a
              message describing the warning condition.

       The possible error values are:

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__AACCTTIIVVAATTEEDD
              The handle has already been activated.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__NNOO__SSUUCCHH__DDEEVVIICCEE
              The capture source specified when the handle was created doesn't
              exist.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__PPEERRMM__DDEENNIIEEDD
              The process doesn't have permission to open the capture source.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__PPRROOMMIISSCC__PPEERRMM__DDEENNIIEEDD
              The process has  permission  to  open  the  capture  source  but
              doesn't have permission to put it into promiscuous mode.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__RRFFMMOONN__NNOOTTSSUUPP
              Monitor  mode  was specified but the capture source doesn't sup‐
              port monitor mode.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__IIFFAACCEE__NNOOTT__UUPP
              The capture source device is not up.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__CCAAPPTTUURREE__NNOOTTSSUUPP
              Packet capture is not supported on the capture source.

       PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR
              Another error occurred.  ppccaapp__ggeetteerrrr() or ppccaapp__ppeerrrroorr()  may  be
              called  with  _p as an argument to fetch or display a message de‐
              scribing the error.

       If  PPCCAAPP__WWAARRNNIINNGG__PPRROOMMIISSCC__NNOOTTSSUUPP,  PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__NNOO__SSUUCCHH__DDEEVVIICCEE,   PPCCAAPP__EERR‐‐
       RROORR__PPEERRMM__DDEENNIIEEDD,     or    PPCCAAPP__EERRRROORR__CCAAPPTTUURREE__NNOOTTSSUUPP    is    returned,
       ppccaapp__ggeetteerrrr() or ppccaapp__ppeerrrroorr() may be called with _p as an  argument  to
       fetch or display an message giving additional details about the problem
       that might be useful for debugging the problem if it's unexpected.

       Additional warning and error codes may be added in the future;  a  pro‐
       gram  should  check  for positive, negative, and zero return codes, and
       treat all positive return codes as warnings  and  all  negative  return
       codes  as errors.  ppccaapp__ssttaattuussttoossttrr(3) can be called, with a warning or
       error code as an argument, to fetch a message describing the warning or
